---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Privacy Policy | Superdots" description="Privacy policy for superdots.sh — how we handle your data.">
	<div class="legal-header">
		<div class="dots dots-md" style="top: 5%; right: 3%;"></div>
		<p class="legal-label">
			<span class="superdot"></span>
			Legal
		</p>
		<h1>Privacy Policy<span class="dot-accent">.</span></h1>
		<p class="legal-updated">Last updated: 16 March 2026</p>
	</div>
	<div class="prose">

		<h2>1. Who we are</h2>
		<p>
			Superdots ("we", "us") operates the website
			<a href="https://superdots.sh">superdots.sh</a> (the "Site").
			For questions about this policy, contact us at
			<a href="mailto:privacy@superdots.sh">privacy@superdots.sh</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>2. What data we collect</h2>
		<p>We collect the minimum data needed to run this Site:</p>
		<table>
			<thead>
				<tr>
					<th>Data</th>
					<th>Purpose</th>
					<th>Legal basis (GDPR)</th>
				</tr>
			</thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr>
					<td>Usage analytics (page views, referrer, device type) via Google Analytics 4</td>
					<td>Understand which content is useful so we can improve the Site</td>
					<td>Consent — Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR</td>
				</tr>
				<tr>
					<td>Theme preference (<code>sd-theme</code> in localStorage)</td>
					<td>Remember your light/dark mode choice</td>
					<td>Legitimate interest — Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR (strictly necessary for the service you requested)</td>
				</tr>
				<tr>
					<td>IP address &amp; server logs (via Cloudflare)</td>
					<td>Deliver pages, protect against abuse</td>
					<td>Legitimate interest — Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR</td>
				</tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
		<p>
			We do <strong>not</strong> collect names, email addresses, or any other personal
			information. There are no user accounts, contact forms, or newsletter sign-ups on this Site.
		</p>

		<h2>3. Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
		<p>
			See our <a href="/cookie-policy">Cookie Policy</a> for the full list of cookies,
			their purposes, durations, and how to manage them.
		</p>

		<h2>4. Third-party data processors</h2>
		<table>
			<thead>
				<tr>
					<th>Service</th>
					<th>Purpose</th>
					<th>Data shared</th>
					<th>Privacy policy</th>
				</tr>
			</thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr>
					<td>Google Analytics 4</td>
					<td>Traffic analytics</td>
					<td>Pseudonymised usage data, IP address (anonymised by default in GA4)</td>
					<td><a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Google Privacy Policy</a></td>
				</tr>
				<tr>
					<td>Google Fonts</td>
					<td>Web fonts (Space Grotesk, Inter, JetBrains Mono)</td>
					<td>IP address, HTTP headers sent with font requests</td>
					<td><a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Google Privacy Policy</a></td>
				</tr>
				<tr>
					<td>Cloudflare Pages</td>
					<td>Hosting, CDN, DDoS protection</td>
					<td>IP address, request metadata</td>
					<td><a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Cloudflare Privacy Policy</a></td>
				</tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>

		<h2>5. International data transfers</h2>
		<p>
			Google and Cloudflare may process data outside the EEA. Both rely on
			Standard Contractual Clauses (SCCs) and, where applicable, the
			EU–US Data Privacy Framework as transfer safeguards. You can review
			Google's transfer mechanisms in their
			<a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy/frameworks" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">data transfer documentation</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>6. Data retention</h2>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Google Analytics data:</strong> retained for 14 months (GA4 default), then automatically deleted.</li>
			<li><strong>localStorage (theme):</strong> persists until you clear your browser data.</li>
			<li><strong>Cloudflare logs:</strong> retained per Cloudflare's standard retention (typically 72 hours for edge logs).</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>7. Your rights</h2>
		<p>Under GDPR (and Italian D.Lgs. 196/2003 as amended by D.Lgs. 101/2018), you have the right to:</p>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Access</strong> the personal data we hold about you (Art. 15 GDPR)</li>
			<li><strong>Rectification</strong> of inaccurate data (Art. 16 GDPR)</li>
			<li><strong>Erasure</strong> ("right to be forgotten") (Art. 17 GDPR)</li>
			<li><strong>Restrict processing</strong> (Art. 18 GDPR)</li>
			<li><strong>Data portability</strong> (Art. 20 GDPR)</li>
			<li><strong>Object</strong> to processing based on legitimate interest (Art. 21 GDPR)</li>
			<li><strong>Withdraw consent</strong> at any time for analytics cookies, without affecting the lawfulness of prior processing (Art. 7(3) GDPR)</li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			To exercise any of these rights, email
			<a href="mailto:privacy@superdots.sh">privacy@superdots.sh</a>.
			We will respond within 30 days.
		</p>

		<h2>8. Complaints</h2>
		<p>
			If you believe your data protection rights have been violated, you may lodge a complaint with:
		</p>
		<ul>
			<li>
				<strong>Garante per la protezione dei dati personali</strong> (Italian Data Protection Authority)<br />
				<a href="https://www.garanteprivacy.it" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">www.garanteprivacy.it</a>
			</li>
			<li>Or your local EU supervisory authority under Art. 77 GDPR.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>9. Changes to this policy</h2>
		<p>
			We may update this policy from time to time. Changes are effective when posted
			on this page. The "Last updated" date at the top reflects the most recent revision.
		</p>

	</div>
</Base>

<style>
	.legal-header {
		position: relative;
		overflow: hidden;
		padding: var(--space-8) 0 var(--space-4);
	}
	.legal-label {
		display: inline-flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: var(--space-2);
		font-family: var(--font-display);
		font-size: var(--text-sm);
		font-weight: var(--weight-semibold);
		text-transform: uppercase;
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
		color: var(--color-primary);
		margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
	}
	.legal-label .superdot {
		width: 8px;
		height: 8px;
		background: var(--color-primary);
		border-radius: var(--radius-full);
		display: inline-block;
	}
	.legal-header h1 {
		margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
	}
	.dot-accent {
		color: var(--color-primary);
	}
	.legal-updated {
		color: var(--color-text-muted);
		font-size: var(--text-sm);
		margin: 0;
	}
	.prose {
		max-width: var(--max-width-prose);
		line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
	}
	.prose h2 {
		font-family: var(--font-display);
		margin-top: var(--space-10);
		margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
	}
	.prose ul {
		padding-left: var(--space-6);
	}
	.prose li {
		margin-bottom: 0.5em;
	}
	.prose li::marker {
		color: var(--color-primary);
	}
	.prose strong {
		color: var(--color-text-strong);
	}
	.prose table {
		width: 100%;
		border-collapse: collapse;
		margin: var(--space-4) 0;
		font-size: var(--text-sm);
	}
	.prose th,
	.prose td {
		text-align: left;
		padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-3);
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
	}
	.prose th {
		font-weight: var(--weight-semibold);
		color: var(--color-text-strong);
	}
	.prose code {
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-size: 0.9em;
		background: var(--color-surface-raised);
		padding: 0.1em 0.3em;
		border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
	}
</style>
